.TH geectl-request-revoke 1  "geectl-request-revoke 0.2.3" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-revoke \- Revoke (withdraw) a submit request, with a comment as the reason
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request revoke\fR [\fB\-\-comment\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIID\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Revoke (withdraw) a submit request, with a comment as the reason
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-comment\fR \fI<COMMENT>\fR [default: ]
The reason for the revocation. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a comment may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIID\fR>
The request id
.SH VERSION
v0.2.3
